From: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Subject: skip the 32-bit assembly sources on amd64
Forwarded: not-needed
Description:
 The 64-bit probe keys off a /system/kernel_x86_64 marker file that
 V\OS does not ship, so the i386-only mmx_gcc.asm and
 Colorcurves_x86.asm were pulled into amd64 builds; nasm -f elf32
 objects cannot link into a 64-bit image. mmx.c already provides the
 x86_64 fallbacks and ColorCurves.cpp guards its gamma_x86 path with
 __INTEL__, so the assembly is dead code here.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>

--- a/source/add-ons/ColorCurves/Jamfile
+++ b/source/add-ons/ColorCurves/Jamfile
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 AS = nasm -f elf32 ;
 
 local have64bits = [ GLOB /system : kernel_x86_64 ] ;
-x86_sources = 	Colorcurves_x86.asm ;
+x86_sources = ;	# Colorcurves_x86.asm is 32-bit only; ColorCurves.cpp has the fallback
 if $(have64bits) {
 	x86_sources = ;
 }
